These factors, according to the VIVIFRAIL programme [ 26 ] include, but are not limited to, the following: myocardial infarction in the past 3 months; unstable angina pectoris; terminal illness; uncontrolled arrhythmia; unstable cardiovascular disease or other unstable medical condition; uncontrolled arterial hypertension; recent pulmonary thromboembolism; upper or lower extremity fracture in the past 3 months; institutionalized or pending entry into institution; and unwillingness to either complete the study requirements or to be randomized into the control or the intervention group.

